The function is declared void, so when it detects an out-of-bounds condition, it calls nvmet_tcp_fatal_error() and returns early without returning any error code to the caller. The callers (e.g., nvmet_tcp_handle_h2c_data_pdu()) proceed to overwrite queue state (queue->rcv_state = NVMET_TCP_RECV_DATA) and attempt to use the uninitialized cmd->recv_msg.msg_iter for network data reception, leading to potential crashes or data corruption.
The code statements that fix the bug are:
