}
Reason:
The function now returns an integer (0 on success, -EPROTO on error) instead of void, explicitly signaling errors to callers. The callers (e.g., nvmet_tcp_handle_h2c_data_pdu()) check the return value and, on failure, jump to the error handling path (e.g., err_proto) which calls nvmet_tcp_fatal_error() and returns -EPROTO, thus preventing the use of an uninitialized iterator and avoiding subsequent issues.

